cards.answer:
Investments by a municipality that improve the quality of life of residents living with a new 220/380 kV high-voltage project, chosen together with those residents.
The grant is a one-off specific grant (specifieke uitkering, money the national government gives a municipality for a set purpose) for municipalities where one of the following is built on land:
- a new 220/380 kV substation;
- a substantial extension of an existing 220/380 kV substation (the area zoned for it grows by at least 100% or at least 5 hectares);
- a new 220/380 kV overhead line of at least 1 kilometre within the municipality.
The project must rest on a project decision or another planning decision under the Environment and Planning Act (Omgevingswet) taken between 1 January 2024 and 31 December 2030, and must appear on the list of eligible projects (about 30, based on the grid operator's Investment Plan 2026). Projects lying wholly on industrial or business land do not qualify. The need comes from residents and local stakeholders: the explanatory notes say the national high-voltage grid must expand sharply, that this weighs on local living conditions, and that falling public support and local resistance cause delays.

The investments must lastingly improve the quality of life of residents near the grid extension, and so help keep regional support for expanding the high-voltage grid.
Examples the call gives:
- green spaces, parks or urban gardens;
- walking and cycling paths, playgrounds and sports facilities;
- renovation of a village or community centre or another meeting place;
- making nearby homes more sustainable, for example collective purchase or subsidy of solar panels, heat pumps or insulation, lowering residents' energy bills.
The explanatory notes link this to the energy transition: without timely grid extension, climate targets slip out of reach and the costs of grid congestion rise. Measures the grid project's developer must take anyway for landscape integration are not eligible; extra measures beyond the legal requirements are.
